---
// The Captive Origins band, in its own palette (brown ink and cream, with a pink accent and
// a little orange, from the public brand notes in the One tools). Everything here is already public: the live
// prototype site and the public One tools. No plans, prices or partners.
---

<section class="co" aria-labelledby="co-title">
  <div class="co-inner">
    <p class="co-eyebrow">What I'm building</p>
    <h2 id="co-title">Captive Origins</h2>
    <p class="co-lede">
      A home for the records of animals in human care, starting with reptiles: what they are,
      where their families come from, and what the sources actually say.
    </p>

    <div class="co-cols">
      <div>
        <h3>Why it's needed</h3>
        <p>
          A lot of captive animals have no reliable record of who their parents were or where
          their line came from. What records there are sit in spreadsheets, on paper cards and in
          people's heads, and they're lost when an animal changes hands. Guesses get passed on as
          facts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>What it does</h3>
        <ul class="co-list">
          <li><strong>Taxonomy</strong> you can browse and search, in your own language.</li>
          <li><strong>Pedigrees</strong> that keep the unknown unknown, instead of filling gaps with guesses.</li>
          <li><strong>Lineage</strong> from genetics, with where the evidence came from and how sure it is.</li>
          <li><strong>Sources cited</strong>, and the people who use it vote on what gets built next.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Why me</h3>
        <p>
          Honestly, it's the project I was always going to end up building. I write software for a
          living, I'm into reptiles, and I lose a lot of nights to old records chasing my own family
          tree. At some point it clicked that a pedigree is just a family tree with scales, and the
          tools I wanted for one would work for the other.
        </p>
        <p>
          How many people are armchair genealogists <em>and</em> into reptiles <em>and</em> software engineers?
          Probably few. I'm one of them, so I'm building it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="co-foot">
      <a class="co-link" href="https://captiveorigins.com">Visit captiveorigins.com</a>
      <span>Early days: the site is a prototype and accounts are invite-only for now. The
      frameworks underneath are source-available, under <a href="#science">Science tools</a>.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Captive Origins palette. Text pairs, the pink accent included, meet WCAG AA; orange is decoration only. */
  .co {
    --co-ink: #4c312c;
    --co-ink-soft: #5e423c;
    --co-bg: #fbf8f2;
    --co-card: #ffffff;
    --co-orange: #cf8137;
    --co-pink: #e48185;
    --co-accent: #b8405e;
    --co-line: #e8dccd;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    background: var(--co-bg);
    color: var(--co-ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--co-line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .co::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    height: 6px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--co-pink), var(--co-accent) 60%, var(--co-orange));
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .co {
      --co-ink: #f3e9df;
      --co-ink-soft: #dccbbd;
      --co-bg: #2a1e1b;
      --co-card: #33241f;
      --co-orange: #e7a066;
      --co-pink: #eda9ac;
      --co-accent: #eda9ac;
      --co-line: #4a3530;
    }
  }
  .co-inner { padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); }
  .co-eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--co-accent);
  }
  .co h2 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.2rem); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .co-lede { margin: 0 0 1.75rem; max-width: 62ch; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .co-cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 17rem), 1fr));
  }
  .co-cols > div {
    background: var(--co-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--co-line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .co h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--co-accent); }
  .co-cols p { margin: 0; }
  .co-cols p + p { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .co-list { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .co-list li { padding-left: 1.1rem; position: relative; margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  .co-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.62em;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--co-accent);
  }
  .co a { color: var(--co-accent); text-decoration-color: var(--co-pink); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
  .co a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 3px; }
  .co-foot { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem; }
  .co-foot span { color: var(--co-ink-soft); }
  .co-link { font-weight: 700; }
</style>
